    {"id":"already-yet","type":"confusable","title":{"en":"already or yet","fi":"already vai yet"},"explanation":{"en":"Already means sooner than expected and goes in the middle: I've already eaten. Yet goes at the end of negatives and questions: I haven't finished yet. Is it ready yet? In US English you also hear the past simple with them: I already ate. Did you eat yet?","fi":"*Already* tarkoittaa jo ja tulee yleensä keskelle lausetta: *I've already eaten*. *Yet* tulee kielteisen lauseen tai kysymyksen loppuun: *I haven't finished yet* (en ole vielä valmis). *Is it ready yet*? (Onko se jo valmis?) Amerikanenglannissa näiden kanssa kuulee myös imperfektiä: *I already ate*. *Did you eat yet*?"},"level":2,"words":[{"text":"already","meaning":{"fi":"jo"}},{"text":"yet","meaning":{"fi":"vielä, jo (kysymyksissä)"}}],"features":["confusable","present-perfect","word-order"]},
