    {"id":"your-youre","type":"confusable","title":{"en":"your or you're","fi":"your vai you're"},"explanation":{"en":"You're is short for you are. Your means belonging to you, like my or his, and has no apostrophe. They sound the same, so the test is: if you can say you are, write you're.","fi":"*you're* = *you are* (sinä olet). *your* = sinun (omistus), aivan kuten *my* ja *his*, eikä siinä ole heittomerkkiä. Sanat kuulostavat samalta, joten testi on tämä: jos voit sanoa *you are*, kirjoita *you're*."},"level":1,"features":["homophone","contraction","possessive"],"words":[{"text":"your"},{"text":"you're"}]},
